\begin{cases} -5 - 3c = -11 \\ 7c - 5a = -16 \\ 3a + 7 = 25 \end{cases}
\] Solving the first equation, we get \(-5 - 3c = -11 \implies -3c = -6 \implies c = 2\). Substituting \(c = 2\) into the second equation, we get \(7(2) - 5a = -16 \implies 14 - 5a = -16 \implies -5a = -30 \implies a = 6\). Substituting \(a = 6\) into the third equation, we get \(3(6) + 7 = 25 \implies 18 + 7 = 25 \implies 25 = 25\), which is true. So, the ordered pair \((a, c)\) is \((6, 2)\). </think> <answer> (6, 2) </answer>

